#: input/pagecontent/workshop-t4.md:63
msgid "Policy · M5Technical · T4PolicyDay 1M1M2M3Day 2M4M5M6M7TechnicalDay 1T1T2T3T4T5Day 2T6T7 Day 1 · 13:50–15:00 · Technical module 4 · serves M5Workflows, sync and who sees whatDraftWhat should happen next for this child, how does the record reach the server, and who is allowed to see it? SessionsTalk13:50–14:00 · 10 minTalk 3: Workflows, sync and who sees whatA short briefing before Lab 2. A plan definition says what should happen and when, such as the next vaccine due. Sync moves records between the device and the server. The gateway decides which records each user can reach.LeadsJing Tang · SupportsElly NandiLab14:00–15:00 · 60 minLab 2: Sync data and run a workflowIn the Player, store records on the device and sync them to the server. Apply an immunization plan definition and see what comes due. Then sign in as two different users through the gateway and compare what each can see, for example 50 records against 10.LeadsElly Nandi, Fikri · SupportsJing Tang By the end you canSync records between the Player and the FHIR serverRead a plan definition and follow it through a workflowShow that the gateway filters records by user Where it meets the journeyJ2bRegistered at home, and referredWhat the system doesEverything Vilay records stays queued on the phone, for up to 28 days, and syncs when a signal returns.Technical questionWhat happens to a queued registration if the clinic registers the same child before the phone syncs?J3bTaifafeki vaccines are fitted to the Onesan scheduleWhat the system doesThe Onesan schedule (PlanDefinition) runs over every dose; at 10 weeks the 6-week doses come out overdue.Technical questionHow does the plan definition decide a dose is overdue, and what sets the date of the next one?J4.0bDad creates a link to share at the clinicWhat the system doesThe family's consent is recorded before the portal issues the link; the gateway enforces passcode, expiry and consent on every request.Technical questionWhere does the gateway read the consent from, and what does it do when the link has expired?J4.1A Taifafeki doctor sees the full historyWhat the system doesEach view is logged as an AuditEvent in Onesa, including failed passcode attempts.Technical questionWhich AuditEvent fields let Onesa tell the family who looked at the record, and when? Technical questions for the roomJ2bWhat happens to a queued registration if the clinic registers the same child before the phone syncs?J3bHow does the plan definition decide a dose is overdue, and what sets the date of the next one?J4.0bWhere does the gateway read the consent from, and what does it do when the link has expired?J4.1Which AuditEvent fields let Onesa tell the family who looked at the record, and when? Terms at those stepsClient RegistryCivil registration and vital statisticsPoint-of-Service ApplicationsFacility, workforce and product registriesConsentInteroperabilityTerminology ServiceCore data setLogical information modelSNOMED CTComputable Decision Support EngineSMART GuidelinesDigital adaptation kitDose number and seriesExpanded Programme on ImmunizationInternational Patient SummaryFast Healthcare Interoperability ResourcesImplementation guideProfileProcurement conditionsApplication programming interfaceGlobal Digital Health Certification NetworkTrust listHealth information exchangeLifelong Health Record M5 Governance, decision rights and the legal basisModule × journey mapAll modules"
